  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: c18dce35c4f218942974316577a84ef5, type: 3}
  m_Name: Scene09_Context
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::OhmsLaw.SceneAgentContext
  sceneId: Scene09
  sceneTitle: Build the Circuit
  askWattsonEnabled: 1
  covered:
  - 'Everything from Scenes 5 to 8: voltage (V, volt) as the push, current (I, ampere),
    Ohm''s investigation, the modern instruments.'
  - The nichrome wire XY is the test conductor; we will change the potential difference
    across it and measure the current through it.
  - The ammeter is connected in series so the same current passes through it and
    the test wire.
  - The voltmeter is connected in parallel across the two ends of the wire, X and
    Y, to measure the potential difference between them.
  - Closing the key completes the circuit so current can flow.
  - "The schematic on the board over the bench shows the same circuit: conventional
    current is drawn from + to \u2212 around the loop; the free electrons themselves
    drift the other way, from \u2212 to +."
  doNotSpoil:
  - The readings
  - The pattern between V and I
  - V is proportional to I
  - V = IR
  - Resistance
  - Ohms
  - The Christmas-lights answer
  faq: {fileID: 11400000, guid: a7cf455846ee290409353722c718ce6a, type: 2}
